# SwiftFormat config. CI runs `swiftformat Sources Tests Tools --lint` with the version
# pinned in .github/workflows/ci.yml; fix locally with `swiftformat Sources Tests Tools`.
--swiftversion 5.9
--indent 4
--maxwidth 120
--exclude .build,Examples/Demo/DerivedData

# A formatter must not change behaviour, public API or test identity. These default rules
# do more than format, so they are off:
# - redundantThrows: drops `throws` from public functions (source/ABI break for callers).
# - redundantRawValues: strips explicit raw values from Codable enums — those strings are
#   the wire contract and stay spelled out.
# - redundantEquatable: deletes hand-written == implementations.
# - swiftTestingTestCaseNames: renames every @Test function (test identity in reports).
# - noForceUnwrapInTests: rewrites test bodies to `try #require`.
# - unusedArguments: renames parameters to `_`.
# - docComments: turns `//` into `///`, changing what DocC publishes.
# - redundantSelf: strips `self.` inside os.Logger interpolations, which are escaping
#   autoclosures that require it — the result does not compile.
# - opaqueGenericParameters: rewrites public `<T: P>` generics as `some P`, a generic
#   signature change flagged by diagnose-api-breaking-changes.
# - redundantInternal: removes explicit `internal`; CONTRIBUTING asks for explicit access control.
--disable redundantThrows,redundantRawValues,redundantEquatable,swiftTestingTestCaseNames,noForceUnwrapInTests,unusedArguments,docComments,redundantSelf,opaqueGenericParameters,redundantInternal
